## Frontend environment variables
## Copy to `.env` and adjust. Restart `npm run dev` after changes.
## Default `npm run dev` runs Vite + local `php -S` (see package.json). For Vite only: `npm run dev:vite`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC SITE URL (production build + SEO)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for sitemap (`npm run build`), JSON-LD absolute URLs, and canonical links
# when you want them fixed regardless of where the HTML is opened.
# Match your deployed static site (no trailing slash).
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://slategrey-hamster-219402.hostingersite.com
#
# Sitemap script also reads `SITE_URL` or `VITE_SITE_URL` from the shell, e.g.:
#   SITE_URL=https://slategrey-hamster-219402.hostingersite.com npm run sitemap

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (PHP API on 127.0.0.1:8000 — started by `npm run dev`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave VITE_ADMIN_PUBLIC_BASE **unset** (or commented out) so the browser
# calls relative `/admin-api`, and Vite proxies that to your local PHP
# (see `vite.config.js`). Then itineraries/hotels read the **same** database
# you see in Admin at 127.0.0.1:8000.
#
# If you set this to a **remote** public.php URL while editing admin locally,
# the site will show the REMOTE package data (often empty itineraries) even
# though your local admin has rows — that is not a migration issue.
#
# Optional explicit local API (same effect as proxy if CORS allows):
# VITE_ADMIN_PUBLIC_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/public.php

# Where Vite proxies /admin-api during `npm run dev` (PHP must be listening here).
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:8000 — start API from repo root, e.g.:
#   cd honeybee_admin && php -S 127.0.0.1:8000
# If ECONNREFUSED: start that server first, or change the port below to match.
# VITE_PHP_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION / STAGED FRONTEND (static build calling live PHP)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prefer `frontend/.env.production` (loaded only for `npm run build`) so local
# `npm run dev` can keep using `/admin-api` without hitting production.
#
# Example — Hostinger admin + static frontend:
#   VITE_ADMIN_PUBLIC_BASE=https://salmon-mole-607064.hostingersite.com/api/public.php
#   VITE_SITE_URL=https://slategrey-hamster-219402.hostingersite.com
#
# On the PHP server (`honeybee_admin/.env`), set CORS to your live frontend origin:
#   HB_APP_CORS_ORIGINS=https://slategrey-hamster-219402.hostingersite.com
# For local dev calling production API, add: ,http://localhost:5173
